  "name": "ok_compaction_txn",
  "description": "The three event types that turn a compaction into a transaction: compaction/start (opened before the summarizer runs), compaction/end (closed with ok true or false), and compaction/summary-error (a summary that could not be produced, so the history stays visible). Additive — no envelope change, no version bump (AGENTS.md rule 2). A start with no end is a compaction that died in flight; this case pins that a reader accepts the bracket and reproduces its bytes.",
